macOS: reuse native thread data within protected operations.

Cider-Topic: sync/msync
Cider-Requires: 0104-msync-thread-local-fork-admission.patch
Cider-Status: nondefault alternative to0105/0106; runtime/performance gates separate
Cider-Review-By: independent scoped signal/reentrancy/lifetime review and parent

Keep the original coordinator, SC fork admission, pending-signal exchange,
leases, transaction/recovery and native frame/cancellation lifetime. Reuse only
function-local pointers to the current native record. There is no new persistent
TLS cache. The per-executor control depth has no independent active writer;
signal handlers only read/defer while it is nonzero. Atomic relaxed load/store
and the original signal fences preserve publication/replay, avoiding an
unneeded shared RMW. This is NOT cross-thread publication; if ownership changes,
this single-writer proof must be revisited. No success acquisition bypasses gate.

